  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a charity campaigner who became paralyzed from the chest down after a riding accident in 2007, has died at the age of 44. She achieved renown for completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days using a bionic suit and raised nearly £1 million for charities through various events. Lomas also lit the Paralympic cauldron in 2012 and participated in the Great North Run in 2016 while pregnant, also wearing her bionic suit. Her family confirmed her death, stating it occurred following an accident in Jordan on August 22nd, and requested privacy for their grief."
